WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.111
Question eight. Highlight: when replaying a chosen period, the system “can jump to” that time — no need to read frame by frame from the start.

00:00:10.111 --> 00:00:13.814
Useful: jump straight to a location = direct access.

00:00:13.814 --> 00:00:18.229
Useless: traffic content itself — does not change access type.

00:00:18.229 --> 00:00:23.854
Option A. Sequential access: must read from the start — opposite of jump — cut.

00:00:23.854 --> 00:00:27.984
Option B. Tape-only serial: stem says disk can jump — cut.

00:00:27.984 --> 00:00:33.182
Option C. Must download whole volume first: stem has no such limit — cut.

00:00:33.182 --> 00:00:35.389
Option D. Direct access — keep.

00:00:35.389 --> 00:00:38.451
Jumping to a chosen frame is direct access.

00:00:38.451 --> 00:00:40.872
Therefore the correct answer is D.
